+      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">The base Multicast VPN (MVPN) specifications, <xref target="RFC6513" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6513"/> and <xref target="RFC6514" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6514"/>, define the &quot;Selective Provider Multicast Service Interface Auto-Discovery route&quot; (S-PMSI A-D route).</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">Per those RFCs, the S-PMSI A-D route contains a Network Layer Reachability Information (NLRI) field that identifies a particular multicast flow.  In the terminology of those RFCs, each flow is denoted by (C-S,C-G), where C-S is an IP source address and C-G is an IP multicast address, both in the address space of a VPN customer.  The (C-S,C-G) of the multicast flow is encoded into the NLRI field.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-3">An S-PMSI A-D route also carries a PMSI Tunnel attribute (PTA).  Typically, the PTA is used to identify a tunnel through the provider backbone network (a &quot;P-tunnel&quot;).</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-4">By originating an S-PMSI A-D route identifying a particular multicast flow and a particular P-tunnel, a node is advertising the following:</t>
+      <blockquote pn="section-1-5">
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-1-5.1">If the node has to transmit packets of the identified flow over the backbone, it will transmit them through the identified tunnel.</t>
