+        <t indent="0" pn="section-3-6.1">For a given C-flow ((C-S,C-G) or (C-*,C-G)), the &quot;match for tracking&quot; is chosen as follows.  Ignore any S-PMSI A-D route that has no PTA.  Also ignore any S-PMSI A-D route whose PTA specifies &quot;no tunnel information present&quot; and has neither the LIR flag nor the LIR-pF flag set.  (That is, <em>do not</em> ignore an S-PMSI A-D route that has a PTA specifying &quot;no tunnel information present&quot; unless its LIR and LIR-pF flags are both clear).  Then apply the rules (from <xref target="RFC6625" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6625"/> and other documents that update it) for finding the &quot;match for reception&quot;.  The result (if any) is the &quot;match for tracking&quot;.</t>
